  "configuration_id": "config_016",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_001 (RNA-only, pca_n2000, singleprofile) achieves 0.485 acc, while config_010 (image-only, resnet50, singleprofile) achieves only 0.208 acc, indicating RNA is the dominant signal and the image modality alone is weak. Key uncertainty: whether the image modality carries complementary information that, when fused with the strong RNA signal, yields a meaningful gain over RNA alone. This is the highest-impact strategic question because it determines whether the 36 multimodal configurations are worth exploring or whether budget should be spent entirely on RNA-side improvements. Config_016 (multimodal, singleprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, concat) is the cleanest test: it combines the exact components already validated in config_001 and config_010 with a simple concatenation fusion, isolating the effect of modality combination. If accuracy exceeds 0.485, multimodal fusion is validated and we can invest in optimizing it; if it does not, we can confidently rule out the resnet50-image branch and redirect budget to RNA encoder/profile improvements (e.g., multiprofile, scvi, scgpt). This single experiment resolves the most consequential design fork under the limited budget."
}

